# Line endings are part of "the same checkout on every machine".
#
# Committed blobs are already LF, but `core.autocrlf=true` — the Git for Windows default —
# rewrites them to CRLF on checkout. So the same commit produces different bytes depending on the
# machine's git config, which is exactly the drift `npm run doctor` exists to catch and this file
# exists to prevent.
#
# It is not cosmetic. `tests/migration-order.test.ts` failed to parse at all —
# `SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token`, zero tests run — because Vitest's transform met a
# shebang terminated by `\r\n` in `scripts/check-migration-order.mjs`. Node imported the same file
# without complaint, so it looked like a test-runner bug rather than a line-ending one.
#
# `eol=lf` wins over whatever `core.autocrlf` each machine has, so neither of us has to remember
# to configure git the same way.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.node binary

# Shell scripts must stay LF or the shebang breaks on the deploy box.
*.sh text eol=lf
